cff-version: "1.2.0"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "SwiftKG: Semantic Knowledge Graph for Swift Codebases"
abstract: >
  SwiftKG builds a hybrid semantic + structural knowledge graph from Swift
  repositories. It indexes every file, class, struct, enum, protocol, actor,
  extension, function, method, property and type alias as a node, with typed
  edges (CALLS, IMPORTS, CONTAINS, INHERITS, CONFORMS, EXTENDS) connecting
  them. A repo-wide two-pass resolver separates superclass inheritance from
  protocol conformance, which Swift writes with identical syntax, and resolves
  references across files, which Swift's module-scoped visibility makes
  correct. Extraction is deterministic tree-sitter parsing, needing no Swift
  toolchain and no buildable project, enabling natural-language querying,
  call-chain analysis, architectural introspection, and MCP-based AI
  integration.
